ationale": "In-paralog baseline moved from the arithmetic mean of an orthogroup's ortholog-PSI distribution to its 10th percentile. On the 417 benchmark pairs whose labels come from UniProt experimental evidence rather than PlantSEED curation, the 10th percentile gives the same precision as any higher baseline (85.7% vs 83.7% at max) with 2.6x the recall (60.3% vs 22.7%)."}
{"date": "2026-09-23", "deltas": {"Athaliana_TAIR10": {"changed": {}, "gained": [], "lost": []}, "Ptrichocarpa_v4.1": {"changed": {}, "gained": [], "lost": ["Potri.005G112150"]}, "Sbicolor_v3.1.1": {"changed": {}, "gained": [], "lost": ["Sobic.001G402800", "Sobic.005G114600", "Sobic.008G137200"]}}, "id": "ortholog-psi-hard-floor", "rationale": "Absolute PSI floor of 0.20 applied to every candidate pair before the O/PAM/PAH branch, so an OrthoFinder ortholog call can no longer bypass all PSI testing. Of 11901 Arabidopsis-Poplar ortholog pairs 8 score exactly 0.00, and the lowest annotation-producing pair is ATCG00070 (chloroplast PsbK) to a nuclear Poplar gene at 0.02. Cost is 4 genes across the three published genomes, all short fragmentary gene models (109-165 aa) matched to full-length references, where PSI is low because of length asymmetry rather than divergence. Measured effect on the in-paralog benchmark is nil: the confusion matrix is bit-identical to no floor and only 5 of 329 baselines move."}
